From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Bongaarts <cab@bongalow.net>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:10:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] 10086: Decompiler Switch Analysis: don't nest switchD
 namespaces under an UndefinedFunction

GP-7316 creates the switchD_ namespace under decompilerResults.getFunction().
For a computed jump outside any defined function that is an UndefinedFunction,
whose getSymbol() throws UnsupportedOperationException when SymbolManager
validates the parent. The exception escapes labelSwitch and aborts the whole
command before the table is disassembled or referenced. Fall back to the
global namespace for an UndefinedFunction, as before GP-7316, and look a
duplicate up under the same parent it was created under.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015RwRYnVtqwZWUAFbFfAhBd
---
 .../app/cmd/function/DecompilerSwitchAnalysisCmd.java       | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/main/java/ghidra/app/cmd/function/DecompilerSwitchAnalysisCmd.java b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/main/java/ghidra/app/cmd/function/DecompilerSwitchAnalysisCmd.java
index 0369fa411f..0707b7297a 100644
--- a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/main/java/ghidra/app/cmd/function/DecompilerSwitchAnalysisCmd.java
+++ b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/main/java/ghidra/app/cmd/function/DecompilerSwitchAnalysisCmd.java
@@ -320,16 +320,18 @@ public class DecompilerSwitchAnalysisCmd extends BackgroundCommand<Program> {
 			}
 		}
 
+		// an UndefinedFunction has no symbol, so it cannot be a namespace parent
 		Function func = decompilerResults.getFunction();
+		Namespace parent = (func instanceof UndefinedFunction) ? null : func;
 
 		// put switch table cases into a new switch namespace
 		Namespace space = null;
 		String switchName = "switchD_" + table.getSwitchAddress();
 		try {
-			space = program.getSymbolTable().createNameSpace(func, switchName, SourceType.ANALYSIS);
+			space = program.getSymbolTable().createNameSpace(parent, switchName, SourceType.ANALYSIS);
 		}
 		catch (DuplicateNameException e) {
-			space = program.getSymbolTable().getNamespace(switchName, null);
+			space = program.getSymbolTable().getNamespace(switchName, parent);
 		}
 		catch (InvalidInputException e) {
 			// just go with default space
